{"1-6":{"people":[{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":1,"firstVerse":1}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0982","lemma":"בָּטַח","tr":"ba·tach","gloss":"to trust","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":120},{"base":"H4862","lemma":"מִשְׁאָלָה","tr":"mish·a·lah","gloss":"petition","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H5243","lemma":"מָלַל","tr":"ma·lal","gloss":"to languish","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H3418","lemma":"יֶ֫רֶק","tr":"ye·req","gloss":"green","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":724},{"base":"H6026","lemma":"עָנֹג","tr":"a·nag","gloss":"to delight","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H1877","lemma":"דֶּ֫שֶׁא","tr":"de·she","gloss":"grass","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H1556","lemma":"גָּלַל","tr":"ga·lal","gloss":"to roll","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H4120","lemma":"מְהֵרָה","tr":"me·he·rah","gloss":"haste","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H2682","lemma":"חָצִיר","tr":"cha·tsir","gloss":"grass","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JHN","chapter":15,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":311,"source":"both","text":"If you remain in Me and My words remain in you, ask whatever you wish, and it will be done for you.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":145,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":245,"source":"both","text":"He fulfills the desires of those who fear Him; He hears their cry and saves them.","from":4},{"book":"ISA","chapter":58,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":180,"source":"both","text":"then you will delight yourself in the LORD, and I will make you ride on the heights of the land and feed you with the heritage of your father Jacob.” For the mouth of the LORD has spoken.","from":4},{"book":"JHN","chapter":15,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":177,"source":"both","text":"You did not choose Me, but I chose you. And I appointed you to go and bear fruit—fruit that will remain—so that whatever you ask the Father in My name, He will give you.","from":4},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":160,"source":"openbible","text":"And this is the confidence that we have before Him: If we ask anything according to His will, He hears us.","from":4},{"book":"1JN","chapter":5,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":160,"source":"openbible","text":"And if we know that He hears us in whatever we ask, we know that we already possess what we have asked of Him.","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":21,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":116,"source":"openbible","text":"O LORD, the king rejoices in Your strength. How greatly he exults in Your salvation!","from":4},{"book":"PSA","chapter":21,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":116,"source":"openbible","text":"You have granted his heartʼs desire and have not withheld the request of his lips. Selah","from":4}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-11":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H2734","lemma":"חָרָה","tr":"cha·rah","gloss":"to be incensed","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":91},{"base":"H7489","lemma":"רָעַע","tr":"ra·a","gloss":"be evil","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":107},{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":231},{"base":"H0408","lemma":"אַל","tr":"al","gloss":"not","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":724},{"base":"H6026","lemma":"עָנֹג","tr":"a·nag","gloss":"to delight","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H0369","lemma":"אַ֫יִן","tr":"a·yin","gloss":"nothing","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":788},{"base":"H4209","lemma":"מְזִמָּה","tr":"me·zim·mah","gloss":"plot","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19},{"base":"H6035","lemma":"עָנָו","tr":"a·nav","gloss":"poor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H1826","lemma":"דָּמַם","tr":"da·mam","gloss":"to silence: stationary","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30},{"base":"H7503","lemma":"רָפָה","tr":"ra·phah","gloss":"to slacken","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":46}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":51,"source":"openbible","text":"Be patient, then, brothers, until the Lordʼs coming. See how the farmer awaits the precious fruit of the soil—how patient he is for the fall and spring rains.","from":7},{"book":"JAS","chapter":5,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":51,"source":"openbible","text":"See how blessed we consider those who have persevered. You have heard of Jobʼs perseverance and have seen the outcome from the Lord. The Lord is full of compassion and mercy.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":27,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":48,"source":"both","text":"Wait patiently for the LORD; be strong and courageous. Wait patiently for the LORD!","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":62,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":43,"source":"openbible","text":"Rest in God alone, O my soul, for my hope comes from Him.","from":7},{"book":"HEB","chapter":10,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":41,"source":"openbible","text":"You need to persevere, so that after you have done the will of God, you will receive what He has promised.","from":7},{"book":"HEB","chapter":10,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":41,"source":"openbible","text":"For, “In just a little while, He who is coming will come and will not delay.","from":7},{"book":"MAT","chapter":5,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":39,"source":"both","text":"Blessed are the meek, for they will inherit the earth.","from":11},{"book":"PRO","chapter":20,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":28,"source":"both","text":"Do not say, “I will avenge this evil!” Wait on the LORD, and He will save you.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-20":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":263},{"base":"H6662","lemma":"צַדִּיק","tr":"tsad·diq","gloss":"righteous","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":206},{"base":"H7198","lemma":"קֶ֫שֶׁת","tr":"qe·shet","gloss":"bow","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":76},{"base":"H7665","lemma":"שָׁבַר","tr":"sha·var","gloss":"to break","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":147},{"base":"H3615","lemma":"כָּלָה","tr":"ka·lah","gloss":"to end: finish","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":208},{"base":"H2719","lemma":"חֶ֫רֶב","tr":"che·rev","gloss":"sword","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":413},{"base":"H7459","lemma":"רְעָבוֹן","tr":"re·a·von","gloss":"famine","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H2786","lemma":"חָרַק","tr":"cha·raq","gloss":"to grind","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":5},{"base":"H2873","lemma":"טָבַח","tr":"ta·vach","gloss":"to slaughter","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":11},{"base":"H2161","lemma":"זָמַם","tr":"za·mam","gloss":"to plan","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":41,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":49,"source":"both","text":"Do not fear, for I am with you; do not be afraid, for I am your God. I will strengthen you; I will surely help you; I will uphold you with My righteous right hand.","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":63,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":45,"source":"both","text":"My soul clings to You; Your right hand upholds me.","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":145,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":44,"source":"both","text":"The LORD upholds all who fall and lifts up all who are bowed down.","from":17},{"book":"ISA","chapter":42,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":39,"source":"both","text":"“Here is My Servant, whom I uphold, My Chosen One, in whom My soul delights. I will put My Spirit on Him, and He will bring justice to the nations.","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":37,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":38,"source":"both","text":"Though he falls, he will not be overwhelmed, for the LORD is holding his hand.","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":116,"verseEnd":116,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"Sustain me as You promised, that I may live; let me not be ashamed of my hope.","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":117,"verseEnd":117,"votes":33,"source":"openbible","text":"Uphold me, and I will be saved, that I may always regard Your statutes.","from":17},{"book":"PSA","chapter":51,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":27,"source":"both","text":"Restore to me the joy of Your salvation, and sustain me with a willing spirit.","from":17}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"21-29":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6662","lemma":"צַדִּיק","tr":"tsad·diq","gloss":"righteous","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":206},{"base":"H2233","lemma":"זֶ֫רַע","tr":"ze·ra","gloss":"seed","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":229},{"base":"H3867","lemma":"לָוָה","tr":"la·vah","gloss":"to join","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":26},{"base":"H2603","lemma":"חָנַן","tr":"cha·nan","gloss":"be gracious","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":78},{"base":"H7931","lemma":"שָׁכַן","tr":"sha·khan","gloss":"to dwell","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":129},{"base":"H5800","lemma":"עָזַב","tr":"a·zav","gloss":"to leave: forsake","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":215},{"base":"H3423","lemma":"יָרַשׁ","tr":"ya·rash","gloss":"to possess: possess","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":231},{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":263},{"base":"H3772","lemma":"כָּרַת","tr":"ka·rat","gloss":"to cut: cut","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":288},{"base":"H4703","lemma":"מִצְעָד","tr":"mits·ad","gloss":"step","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":16,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":68,"source":"both","text":"A manʼs heart plans his course, but the LORD determines his steps.","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":133,"verseEnd":133,"votes":57,"source":"both","text":"Order my steps in Your word; let no sin rule over me.","from":23},{"book":"PRO","chapter":4,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":48,"source":"both","text":"Make a level path for your feet, and all your ways will be sure.","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":40,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":44,"source":"both","text":"He lifted me up from the pit of despair, out of the miry clay; He set my feet upon a rock, and made my footsteps firm.","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":121,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":40,"source":"both","text":"The LORD will watch over your coming and going, both now and forevermore.","from":23},{"book":"1SA","chapter":2,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":39,"source":"both","text":"He guards the steps of His faithful ones, but the wicked perish in darkness; for by his own strength shall no man prevail.","from":23},{"book":"PSA","chapter":85,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":37,"source":"both","text":"Righteousness will go before Him to prepare the way for His steps.","from":23},{"book":"JER","chapter":10,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":35,"source":"both","text":"I know, O LORD, that a manʼs way is not his own; no one who walks directs his own steps.","from":23}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"30-34":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H6662","lemma":"צַדִּיק","tr":"tsad·diq","gloss":"righteous","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":206},{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":263},{"base":"H4571","lemma":"מָעַד","tr":"ma·ad","gloss":"to slip","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H0838","lemma":"אֲשׁוּר","tr":"a·shur","gloss":"step","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":9},{"base":"H1897","lemma":"הָגָה","tr":"ha·gah","gloss":"to mutter","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":25},{"base":"H7561","lemma":"רָשַׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"be wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34},{"base":"H6822","lemma":"צָפָה","tr":"tsa·phah","gloss":"to watch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":35},{"base":"H6960","lemma":"קָוָה","tr":"qa·vah","gloss":"to await","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":49},{"base":"H3956","lemma":"לָשׁוֹן","tr":"la·shon","gloss":"tongue","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":117},{"base":"H2451","lemma":"חׇכְמָה","tr":"chokh·mah","gloss":"wisdom","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":153}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":27,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"Wait patiently for the LORD; be strong and courageous. Wait patiently for the LORD!","from":34},{"book":"PSA","chapter":40,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"I delight to do Your will, O my God; Your law is within my heart.”","from":31},{"book":"PRO","chapter":20,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Do not say, “I will avenge this evil!” Wait on the LORD, and He will save you.","from":34},{"book":"COL","chapter":4,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Let your speech always be gracious, seasoned with salt, so that you may know how to answer everyone.","from":30},{"book":"DEU","chapter":6,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"These words I am commanding you today are to be upon your hearts.","from":31},{"book":"PSA","chapter":37,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"For the evildoers will be cut off, but those who hope in the LORD will inherit the land.","from":34},{"book":"PRO","chapter":25,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"A word fitly spoken is like apples of gold in settings of silver.","from":30},{"book":"PRO","chapter":25,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":10,"source":"openbible","text":"Like the cold of snow in the time of harvest is a trustworthy messenger to those who send him; he refreshes the soul of his masters.","from":30}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"35-40":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H7563","lemma":"רָשָׁע","tr":"ra·sah","gloss":"wicked","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":263},{"base":"H6403","lemma":"פָּלַט","tr":"pa·lat","gloss":"to escape","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":26},{"base":"H0319","lemma":"אַחֲרִית","tr":"a·cha·rit","gloss":"end","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":61},{"base":"H6168","lemma":"עָרָה","tr":"a·rah","gloss":"to uncover","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H8535","lemma":"תָּם","tr":"tam","gloss":"complete","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H0249","lemma":"אֶזְרָח","tr":"ez·rach","gloss":"born","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":17},{"base":"H6184","lemma":"עָרִיץ","tr":"a·rits","gloss":"ruthless","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H7488","lemma":"רָעַן","tr":"ra·an","gloss":"be fresh","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H8668","lemma":"תְּשׁוּעָה","tr":"te·shu·ah","gloss":"deliverance: salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":34},{"base":"H4581","lemma":"מָעוֹז","tr":"ma·oz","gloss":"security","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":36}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":32,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"The work of righteousness will be peace; the service of righteousness will be quiet confidence forever.","from":37},{"book":"PSA","chapter":9,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"The LORD is a refuge for the oppressed, a stronghold in times of trouble.","from":39},{"book":"PSA","chapter":91,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"When he calls out to Me, I will answer him; I will be with him in trouble. I will deliver him and honor him.","from":39},{"book":"PSA","chapter":37,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Yet a little while, and the wicked will be no more; though you look for them, they will not be found.","from":36},{"book":"ISA","chapter":31,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Like birds hovering overhead, so the LORD of Hosts will protect Jerusalem. He will shield it and deliver it; He will pass over it and preserve it.”","from":40},{"book":"ISA","chapter":57,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"The righteous perish, and no one takes it to heart; devout men are taken away, while no one considers that the righteous are taken away from the presence of evil.","from":37},{"book":"ISA","chapter":57,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Those who walk uprightly enter into peace; they find rest, lying down in death.","from":37},{"book":"JOB","chapter":5,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"I have seen a fool taking root, but suddenly his house was cursed.","from":35}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}